{"id": "86313", "name": "מקדמים קבועים הומוגנית – בעיית התחלה של ay″ + by = 0 (ב) (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Solve</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} + {{CT:1}} y = 0,\\ y(0) = {{CT:2}},\\ y^\\prime(0) = {{CT:3}} \\]</p><p>where \\({}^\\prime\\) denotes differentiation with respect to \\(x\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(y(x) =\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Substitute \\(y=e^{mx}\\) to get the auxiliary equation; its imaginary roots give a combination of cosine and sine, and the initial conditions fix A and B.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The auxiliary equation</b><br>To solve the differential equation<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} + {{CT:1}} y = 0 \\]</p>Let \\(y = e^{mx}\\) and hence \\(\\frac{dy}{dx}=me^{mx}\\) and \\(\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = m^2e^{mx}\\). Substituting for \\(y\\) gives<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}m^2e^{mx} + {{CT:1}}e^{mx} = 0 \\]</p>and dividing throughout by \\(e^{mx}\\) (never zero) and {{CT:4}} gives the auxiliary (characteristic) equation<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ m^2 + {{CT:5}} = 0 \\]</p>which can be solved to give {{CT:6}}: purely imaginary roots.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The general solution</b><br>For roots of \\(m\\) in the form \\(a±bi\\), the solution to the differential equation is of the form<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y = {{CT:7}}(A\\cos(bx)+B\\sin(bx)) \\]</p>Here \\(a=0\\) and \\(b={{CT:8}}\\), and therefore<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y= A\\cos({{CT:9}})+B\\sin({{CT:9}}) \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The initial conditions</b><br>Given \\(\\ y(0) = {{CT:2}}\\), substituting \\(x=0\\) gives<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[  A = {{CT:2}} \\]</p>and given \\(\\ y^\\prime(0) = {{CT:3}}\\), differentiating (\\(y^\\prime(0)={{CT:8}}B\\)) gives<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ B = {{CT:10}} \\]</p>Therefore<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y = {{CT:11}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 30, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 2, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, 